IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-rules`
IMPORT `wills-seat`

-- Wills Act 2000 (NT) -- worked cases for the will-maker's questions (wills-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the will-maker`

§§ `s 6 -- can I leave this property by my will`

#ASSERT `Can I leave this property by my will` `I am entitled to it at my death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I leave this property by my will` `my personal representative becomes entitled to it, as personal representative, after my death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I leave this property by my will` `I hold it as trustee at my death` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I leave this property by my will` `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 7, 18 -- is my will valid as to my age`

-- Arguments: age, marital status, in contemplation of a marriage, Court order under Part 3.
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 18 `never married` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am 18 or over`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 40 `married now` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am 18 or over`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `married now` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am a married minor (s 7(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 7(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under Part 3`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `married now` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under Part 3`
-- A widowed or divorced minor may revoke (s 7(2)(c)) but not make a new will (finding 8).
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 16 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 7(2)(a))`

§§ `ss 7, 18 -- can I revoke my will as a minor`

-- Arguments: age, marital status, made in contemplation of marriage, made while married, Court order.
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 18 `never married` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married now` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 18(2) -- can the Court authorise my will as a minor`

-- Arguments: age, understands, reflects intentions, reasonable.
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 18 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18(4) -- is my Court-authorised will as a minor valid`

-- Arguments: executed as the Act requires, the Registrar a witness, follows the order's conditions.
#ASSERT `Is my Court-authorised will as a minor valid` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my Court-authorised will as a minor valid` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my Court-authorised will as a minor valid` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my Court-authorised will as a minor valid` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 8, 9, 11 -- is my will validly signed and witnessed`

-- Arguments: in writing, who signed, intending, witnesses present together (able to see), of them how many signed.
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 3 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A third person who signs but was not present at the signing does not make up the two (s 8(1)(c), "those witnesses").
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 1 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `someone else signed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `nobody signed it` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` FALSE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` FALSE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 46 -- is my will made under another law properly executed`

-- Arguments: law of the place made, of domicile or habitual residence, of nationality, of the vessel's place.
#ASSERT `Is my will made under another law properly executed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made under another law properly executed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made under another law properly executed` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made under another law properly executed` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made under another law properly executed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 5A and the Annex -- is my will valid as an international will`

-- Arguments: one person's will, in writing, authorised person, witnesses, declared, signed, attested.
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `a public notary of an Australian jurisdiction, acting in Australia` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `a person authorised under the law of another country that is party to the Convention` 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `nobody authorised` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` FALSE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as an international will` TRUE TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 13 -- is my will revoked`

#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I made a later will that revokes it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I signed a writing declaring I revoke it, executed like a will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I burned, tore or destroyed it, intending to revoke it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `someone else destroyed it in my presence, at my direction, with my intention to revoke it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `someone else destroyed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `it was destroyed by accident or without an intention to revoke it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I wrote on it or dealt with it so that the Court is satisfied from its state that I intended to revoke it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `the Court ordered it revoked under Part 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I said or wrote that I revoke it, without executing the writing like a will` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will revoked` `I made a later will that does not revoke it` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 14 -- what does my marriage do to my will`

-- Arguments: married since, in contemplation of that marriage, expressed in contemplation of marriage generally.
#ASSERT `What does my marriage do to my will` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 14 does not arise: I have not married since I made the will`
#ASSERT `What does my marriage do to my will` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 14(3))`
#ASSERT `What does my marriage do to my will` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not revoked: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 14(4))`
#ASSERT `What does my marriage do to my will` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death (s 14(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `What does my marriage do to my will` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not revoked: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 14(3))`

§§ `s 15 -- does my divorce revoke this part of my will`

-- Arguments: how the marriage ended, the part of the will, contrary intention.
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `my former spouse's appointment as executor, guardian or advisory trustee` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `my former spouse's appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include my former spouse's children` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `my former spouse's appointment as trustee of other property` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `a power of appointment my former spouse may exercise only in favour of our children` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `another power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `a part that does not concern my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` `a gift to my former spouse` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a decree of nullity was granted by the Family Court` `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `dissolved or annulled outside Australia, and recognised in Australia under the Family Law Act 1975` `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `dissolved or annulled outside Australia, but not recognised in Australia` `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Separation alone: the gift stands until a divorce (finding 2).
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `we separated, but the marriage has not been dissolved or annulled` `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 -- is my change to my will effective`

-- Arguments: made after execution, how it was made.
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `signed by me and witnessed like a will (signatures may be in the margin or on a memorandum)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `made as a minor under a Court order under s 18(1), as the order requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `made for me under a Court order under s 19(1), while I lacked testamentary capacity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `the Court is satisfied under s 10 that it embodies my intentions (after my death)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `I obliterated words so that their effect is no longer apparent` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE `none of these (for example, initialled by me only, or not witnessed)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` FALSE `none of these (for example, initialled by me only, or not witnessed)` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 17 -- is my revoked will revived`

#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` `I re-executed the revoked will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` `I executed a will showing an intention to revive it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` `something else (for example, I taped the torn will together, or I said it should stand)` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 50 -- depositing my will`

#ASSERT `Can my will be deposited in this envelope` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my will be deposited in this envelope` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: why it is deposited, fee waived.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the will deposit fee` `I am depositing my own will` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the will deposit fee` `I am depositing my own will` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the will deposit fee` `a Court-authorised will under Part 3` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the will deposit fee` `my lawyer has died, or has ceased or is about to cease practising law in the Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 25(2), 51 -- can I get my deposited will back`

-- Arguments: age, capacity now, a will made by Court order while lacking capacity, revocation order, applied in writing.
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 18 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A revocation order lifts the s 25(2) bar, but s 51(2) still withholds the will from a testator who lacks capacity
-- (finding 7, fork F11).
#ASSERT `Can I get my deposited will back` 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
